WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:02.548
(vocalizing)

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:04.863
- Look at him.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:08.154
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.510
I think the song I
enjoyed crafting the most

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.333
in the documentary is Perfect.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.550
That's my favorite song I've done.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.390
I think it was the first song
that I wrote for the album,

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.730
so I think it was just when I knew

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.813
that the album was sort of done.

00:00:26.813 --> 00:00:29.396
(upbeat music)

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.320
Yeah, well I think, I think,
I think there're like loads.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.720
Someone like Kendrick Lamar.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.060
Drake's obviously doing very, very well.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.790
I really like Taylor's album.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.040
Ariana Grande just brought
out that song God is A Woman

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.870
which is an amazing bit of pop music,

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:46.030
so every week you hear
something that inspires you

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.043
to be better, I think.

00:00:48.304 --> 00:00:50.887
(upbeat music)

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.710
I don't really know 'cause I've only done

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.630
two songs with her, I've never really done

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.070
any other studio time,

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.970
but I think, you know, I think
she's quite a similar writer.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.050
I think she writes from her
own personal experiences

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.965
and tries to make the songs
as honest as possible.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.548
(upbeat music)

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.793
No, no I don't think,

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.583
don't think her cats have been to England.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.460
Maybe they have, I don't know.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.820
I can't fly with my cats anywhere,

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.403
'cause they just don't
really like moving anywhere.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.560
They're just home cats.

00:01:22.688 --> 00:01:25.271
(upbeat music)

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.300
Sherry, but Sherry's actually here today

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.160
'cause she's got a
couple of weeks off work.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.184
So at the moment, my
mom and dad have them.

00:01:31.184 --> 00:01:33.767
(upbeat music)

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.457
There's an artist (laughs) called Labrinth

00:01:37.891 --> 00:01:40.432
that wrote a song called
Jealous, and I love that.

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:43.015
(upbeat music)

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.490
I think you need a little bit of both.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:47.330
I always song write whilst I'm on tour.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.273
So I can have a balance.

00:01:49.273 --> 00:01:51.856
(upbeat music)

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.360
I think writer's block doesn't exist

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.000
if you continually keep writing.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.453
I think if you always write songs,

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.750
it doesn't matter how
good or bad they are,

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.343
you just write them.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.220
I think the only time I've experienced

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.480
anything close to writer's block

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.993
is having, like, a long
time off not writing.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.330
And then it's kind of getting back

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.097
into the swing of things.

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:14.170
(upbeat music)

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.220
So there's a songwriter called Max Martin

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.513
who I was with in Sweden recently,

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.563
and he wrote Everybody
for Backstreet Boys.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.010
And I went round his house

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.020
and he had a taco night on a Friday,

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.898
and he came up to me with the taco singing

00:02:27.898 --> 00:02:29.830
♪ Taco Friday ♪

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.143
and I just sing that every now and then.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:35.600
I keep telling him, like,
someone like Taco Bell

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:39.840
should like approach him and
use that song as a campaign.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.590
Can you imagine that as like
a huge Taco Bell campaign?

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.505
Every Friday is

00:02:43.505 --> 00:02:45.195
♪ Taco Friday ♪

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.173
And it's like, you know, two
for one tacos at Taco Bell.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.153
You're welcome.

00:02:49.176 --> 00:02:51.759
(upbeat music)

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.080
Do you know what, I always thought

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.363
I'd probably be Hufflepuff.

00:02:56.363 --> 00:02:58.640
Sytherin's like pure pure-blood

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.800
and I'm kind of like mixed
between Irish and English,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.100
and Ravenclaw's very smart,
Gryffindor's like really like

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.870
brave and (growls) and
Hufflepuff's just kind of the one

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.309
that isn't so I guess I'd be Hufflepuff.

00:03:11.309 --> 00:03:13.892
(upbeat music)

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.650
I know what Game of Thrones fans

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.163
hope happened to my character.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.070
I'm sure they think my character

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.900
got brutally, brutally murdered,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.863
but I think my character
is still out there.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.203
I think he's chilling
(laughs) like the cat.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.750
Yeah, it was fun.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.780
It was fun being in Game of Thrones,

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:35.380
but I definitely think they
should've killed me off

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.213
in the episode.

00:03:36.213 --> 00:03:37.290
I reckon that probably
would've been, like,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.348
the redemption of people
who didn't like it.

00:03:39.348 --> 00:03:41.931
(upbeat music)

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.060
Yeah, it's always like it's either

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.010
Goodfellas or Cool Runnings
and I don't know which one.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.430
They both do different things, don't they?

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.980
I think the movie I've seen
the most is Goodfellas.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.503
So probably Goodfellas.

00:03:52.528 --> 00:03:54.720
(upbeat music)

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.980
I now view my tattoos as one tattoo

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.383
'cause it's just kind of one thing.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.090
So, I just like my tattoo.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.673
(upbeat music)

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.000
I always loved painting as a kid,

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.833
so I think I'd probably be
something to do with art.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:10.947
Yeah, something creative.

00:04:10.947 --> 00:04:13.530
(upbeat music)

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:19.100
You have to be prepared
for like five to six years

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.420
of overnight success if that makes sense.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.950
You have to like do loads of stuff

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.773
that no one notices at all,

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.360
and that's like five, six years minimum.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.863
You have to like play gigs
that no one listens to,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.743
write songs that everyone
doesn't believe in,

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.810
and just like just
believe in yourself enough

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:36.660
and then just never have a plan B.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.270
Always think that you are gonna succeed

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.520
and eventually you are.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.630
If you wish success into
existence, basically,

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.740
and just believe in yourself,

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.140
and don't after six years be like

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:47.580
oh do you know what I'm just gonna go

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.570
and get a desk job or something.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.090
If you wanna be a musician, be a musician.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.370
Because you can always make
a living being a musician.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.450
So, these kittens are here today

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:56.313
through Best Friends Animal Society.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.690
And it's kitten season right now,

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.533
so means there's loads of
kittens that don't have homes.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.973
And if they don't get homes,
bad things happen to them.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.863
So, please adopt cute kittens like these.

00:05:07.016 --> 00:05:09.913
Bestfriends.org, go on it,
find yourself a kitten.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.570
Maybe don't even get a kitten,

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:13.790
maybe get an older cat that
needs a bit of love as well

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:14.896
'cause all cats need love.

00:05:14.896 --> 00:05:17.479
(upbeat music)

